class.description:
A [FlowNode] is one step of a [FlowGraph]. It defines its ports ([FlowPort]), its title and category, and warnings about its configuration. The graph owns the node ids; a node itself does not know its id. Use [method FlowGraph.find_node_id] to get it.
[b]Node types.[/b] The built-in node types ([FlowStartNode], [FlowEndNode], [FlowBranchNode], [FlowExpressionNode], [FlowGetVariableNode], [FlowSetVariableNode], [FlowEmitEventNode], [FlowSubgraphNode], [FlowWaitNode]) are subclasses. You add your own node types by extending [FlowNode] in GDScript, in C# (with [code][GlobalClass][/code]) or in C++ (GDExtension), and overriding the virtual methods below. Use properties for the settings of the node; they are saved with the graph like those of any resource. If your node needs different ports after a property changed, call [method notify_ports_changed].
[b]Ports.[/b] The ports are asked for once and cached. Call [method notify_ports_changed] when the result of [method _get_input_ports] or [method _get_output_ports] changes. A script override takes precedence over the ports of a built-in node type.
[b]Ownership.[/b] A node belongs to at most one graph. [method FlowGraph.add_node] refuses a node that is still in another graph (or already in the same one); remove it with [method FlowGraph.remove_node] first, or add a [code]duplicate()[/code] of it.
[b]Runtime.[/b] A [FlowGraphPlayback] runs the graph and calls the runtime virtual methods: [method _enter] when the node becomes current, [method _choose_exit] to pick the flow output, [method _exit] when it is left, [method _evaluate_output] when another node reads one of its data outputs, [method _process_waiting] each frame while it waits, and [method _get_available_exits] for choice menus. They are [code]const[/code]: a node resource is shared by every playback of its graph, so keep runtime data in [method FlowGraphPlayback.set_node_memory] or in variables, not in properties. Read data inputs with [method FlowGraphPlayback.get_input_value].
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
class_name HasItemNode
extends FlowNode

func _get_input_ports() -> Array[FlowPort]:
	return [FlowPort.create_flow("in"), FlowPort.create_data("item", TYPE_STRING)]

func _get_output_ports() -> Array[FlowPort]:
	return [FlowPort.create_flow("yes"), FlowPort.create_flow("no")]

func _get_category() -> String:
	return "Inventory"

func _get_inline_properties() -> PackedStringArray:
	return PackedStringArray(["title_override"])
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
[GlobalClass]
public partial class HasItemNode : FlowNode
{
    public override Godot.Collections.Array<FlowPort> _GetInputPorts()
    {
        return new Godot.Collections.Array<FlowPort>
        {
            FlowPort.CreateFlow("in"),
            FlowPort.CreateData("item", Variant.Type.String),
        };
    }

    public override Godot.Collections.Array<FlowPort> _GetOutputPorts()
    {
        return new Godot.Collections.Array<FlowPort>
        {
            FlowPort.CreateFlow("yes"),
            FlowPort.CreateFlow("no"),
        };
    }

    public override string _GetCategory() => "Inventory";
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
